  note = {Fermionic matter sub-programme source note: recasts the charged-lepton Koide relation as a unit coefficient-of-variation condition on the square-root mass vector, $Q_\ell=(1+\mathrm{CV}(r_\ell)^2)/3$, hence $Q_\ell=2/3 \iff \mathrm{CV}(r_\ell)=1$ ($\sigma_r=\bar r$); separates the dispersion constraint from the hierarchy phase (node placement); records the dispersion obstruction $\mathrm{CV}\le 1/\sqrt2$, $Q\le 1/2$ of the cascade ladder, taken by hypothesis as a pinned normal form; states the maximum-entropy reading as an open $S_\Pi$-variational test. Target invariant for the fermionic-mass sector, not a mass formula.
